373:## 5. The CHANGELOG block (verbatim)
374:```
375:# `#567` (fbctrlcmdkill): the test machines' framebuffer controller ended the emulator on any command but NOP, SET_RESOLUTION and GET_RESOLUTION, and ran a WIDE value as its low word -- every other 64-bit value at COMMAND is refused before the store now, COMMAND kept, one announce per device; with a 125-row rung-3 detector, gated in gate 16; held for Fable
376:
377:**The defect** (filed by `#549`'s review, `fbctrlcmdkill`, HIGH).  `fbctrl_command()`'s `default:` called `fatal()`
378:then `exit(1)` for every command other than NOP (0), SET_RESOLUTION (1) and GET_RESOLUTION (2) -- FILL (3) and COPY (4)
379:included, which `dev_fb.h` names under a bare `TODO:` with no port semantics.  A guest reaches it with ONE DATA write
380:while COMMAND (port 0, the power-on selector) is selected, on every test machine (`machine_test.c` installs
381:`fbctrl addr=0x12f00000`).  And `d->port[]` is `int`, so a wide `sd` was stored as its low word and DISPATCHED:
382:`0x100000003` ended the emulator as FILL, and `0x100000001` silently ran SET_RESOLUTION.  Witness, rung 3 on an
383:unmodified `-E testmips` with HEAD's binary: 2/12 -- 3, 4, 5, -1 and `sd 0x100000003` each exit 1
384:(`regress/artifacts/fbctrlcmdkill/pass1_20261018/WITNESS_headbin.out`); 12/12 on the fix.
385:
386:**What ships.**
387:* `src/devices/dev_fbctrl.c` -- the DATA arm refuses, BEFORE the store, any write at COMMAND whose full 64-bit value is
388:  above GET_RESOLUTION: COMMAND keeps its previous value, nothing executes, and a new `warned_cmd` latch prints one
389:  `[ fbctrl: command 0x... is not supported; the command port is unchanged (once) ]` per device.  `fbctrl_command()`'s
390:  `default:` stays, unreachable, as a tripwire (as `#549` kept the selector's).  `est/` byte-identical; `build/`,
391:  `build-asan/` and `/tmp/gxsec-build` rebuilt and cleared both parts.
392:* `regress/fbctrl_cmd_probe.py` (new, 125 rows, 27 sessions on an unmodified `-E testmips`) -- eleven refusal classes
393:  (3, 4, 5 and `0xffffffff` by `sw`; 3 by `sb`, 4 by `sh`; `0x100000003`, the three wide aliases of accepted commands
394:  and all-ones by `sd`) on a device seeded with COMMAND = 2, X1 = 123, Y1 = 77; the bound's two edges -- 2 accepted with
395:  an observable dispatch, 3 refused -- at every access width, with the latch clear and set; reads and non-COMMAND stores
396:  at every width; the latch across an accept and a read; the selector's latch apart from it in both orders; one
397:  free-running session for the announce level.  Its CONTRACT is its header -- the floor, the width cells held, the
398:  effects, and NOT CLAIMED (0)-(7), (7) being the observation cells pass 3 named and the owner filed as debt.
399:* `regress/gate_mips_folds.sh` (gate 16) -- the probe's block beside `#549`'s, before the pmax-kernel check: parse
400:  before score; CONTROL `OK`; exit 0; the score pinned by EQUALITY at 125; rows emitted, green rows and unique names
401:  reconciled with one anchored pattern (this probe prints a row's status after got/want); and EVERY expected row checked
402:  by name, green exactly once.
403:* `regress/gate_hygiene.sh` -- `EXPECT_PTY_PROBES` 75 -> 76 and `EXPECT_CONVERTED` 25 -> 26 for this probe (`#564`'s own
404:  stranded pin landed alone, in the commit before this one).
405:* `tools/precommit_check.sh` -- `SCORE_CLAIMS_MANIFEST` 35 -> 36 (`fbctrl_cmd rows run ... 125`).
406:* `tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py` -- the probe's MANIFEST line.
407:* `tools/pipeline/ledger.json` -- `fbctrlcmdkill` HELD for fable5 (Fable walled on every pass; a row may not close while
408:  a stage awaits a seat); FILES `fbctrlobsgrid` (MED: pass 3's observation cells), `fbctrlvec128` (LOW: a 16-byte vector
409:  store is taken as its low 64 bits, at DATA and at `#549`'s PORT) and `gate16fence` (LOW: gate 16 launches both device
410:  probes unfenced); `gatedevicesplit` gains the gate-16 stop -- a third device probe lands there only with the split or
411:  with a pin on the launch count.
412:
413:**Measured** (`regress/artifacts/fbctrlcmdkill/`; every table's predictions written first, in a `PRETABLE*` file whose
414:mtime is the order proof).
415:* The draft (`draft_20261018/`): PRE-FIX 36/95 on HEAD's binary -- exactly the PRETABLE's prediction -- and 95/95 on
416:  the fix.
417:* Kill tables 1 and 1b (`killtable1_20261018/`, `killtable1b_20261018/`): sixteen mutants on the 95-row v1, all red;
418:  clause (b) `B_gateoff` (the arm as HEAD has it) row for row the pre-fix leg; clause (c) measured -- an absent and a
419:  non-emulator binary each CONTROL=FAILED.
420:* Pass 2's mutants, measured BEFORE any repair (table 2a): three passed v1 whole; probe v2 (99 rows) closed them and
421:  table 2 re-ran all 25: every one red.  F2's, measured before any repair (table 3a): seven passed v2 whole; probe v3
422:  (106 rows) closed them and table 3 re-ran all 32: every one red, every prediction held.
423:* Two consecutive passes had found one class open -- access WIDTH -- so v4 (123 rows) was built from an enumeration
424:  written before it ran (`killtable4_20261019/PRETABLE_ADDENDUM_t4.out`).  **Table 4** (06:30-07:03): the twelve
425:  newest mutants passed the 106-row v3 whole, and on v4 all 44 are red; legs 123/123 on the fix and 51/123 on HEAD's
426:  binary; both null media CONTROL=FAILED; every prediction held row for row (`KILLTABLE4_VS_PRETABLE.out`).
427:* Pass 3 found the v4 enumeration counted cells REACHED, not every effect OBSERVED; by the owner's ruling two rows were
428:  added from values R:edges already collected (`edge x1`, `edge y1`), and plain regression runs measured the 125-row
429:  probe: the fix 125/125, HEAD's build 51/125, both null media 17/125 with CONTROL=FAILED (`killtable4_20261019/legs41/`).
430:* Gate 16 run IN SITU (`wiring_20261019/INSITU.md`): on the default binary PASS, 161 checks; on HEAD's binary FAIL, 77 of
431:  161, every red check this block's.  The v4 block replayed on all 48 table-4 logs and five broken logs was green only
432:  on the fix (`GATE16_REPLAY_v4.out`).
433:* The weekly battery of 2026-10-18 (re-run at 23:19 after Modern Standby killed the 18:00 run) passed 16/16 with
434:  `#567`'s first, 95-row block in gate 16; the block that ships is the 125-row one, run in situ above.
435:
436:**Panel.**  Pass 1 (`pass1_20261018/`): GPT-6 Astra, Grok 4.7 and GLM 5.3 chose member 3 (decline + latched announce),
437:the full 64-bit compare and a new gated probe; `fbctrloffkill` stays its own row (2-1).  Pass 2 (`pass2_20261018/`): all
438:three SHIP WITH CHANGES.  F2 (`pass2_20261018/f2/F2_DISPOSITIONS.md`): all three SHIP WITH CHANGES, converging on width x
439:bound edge and the latch's persistence.  Records corrected on the way, each a seat's catch: NOT CLAIMED (6) put the
440:16-byte loss in the wrong place (Astra, Grok); testppc's install is `machine_test.c`'s line 154, not 337 (Astra, Grok);
441:E8 sets the latch on an accept (GLM); GET_RESOLUTION makes four X1/Y1 assignments (Astra, Grok); v2's bound edges were
442:held at `sb` and `sw`.  Pass 3 (`pass3_20261019/F3_DISPOSITIONS.md`): GPT-6 Astra, GLM 5.3 and Grok 4.7 all SHIP WITH CHANGES -- the width enumeration counted cells reached, not every effect observed; by the owner's ruling two rows were added (`edge x1`, `edge y1`), the remaining cells filed as `fbctrlobsgrid`, and the records corrected (the gate comment, the probe's width list and NOT CLAIMED (2), (5) and (7)).  Confirm (GPT-6 Astra): requested on this unit.
443:Fable 5.1 walled (HTTP 429) on passes 1, 2, F2 and 3 -- each a seat failure, held with its question, never agreement;
444:the row is held for it.  Opus 5.5, agy, kimi, deepseek and minimax deliberately not fired (the owner's 2026-10-17
