 entry it pointed at. ***  widthkillclass was the one CORRECT clearance: held at review, all seven named seats answered at review.  A strictly-later + same-stage test keeps all six and clears that one.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">gxprobepccache</span><span class="ttl">gxprobe cached the pc across `step`, so a driver that stepped without _exec_at() had its next pc assignment silently skipped -- a detector row that could not fail</span><span class="tip">gxprobe cached the pc across `step`, so a driver that stepped without _exec_at() had its next pc assignment silently skipped -- a detector row that could not fail — witness: harness:MEASURED by the #497-family measuring seat and re-verified here.  `gxprobe.py` skips a redundant register assignment when `cache_regs` is on; `_exec_at()` pops the cached pc after stepping, but a driver calling `send(&quot;step&quot;)` DIRECTLY did not -- so its next `set_reg(&quot;pc&quot;, a)` was dropped as redundant.  The transcript is unambiguous: the first access carries a `pc=` line, the second and third do not, and they execute `nop`.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">pcc2widthkills</span><span class="ttl">dev_pcc2.c: TEN live width kills (of twelve guards -- #119 already fixed two in this same file, and its shape is the answer)</span><span class="tip">dev_pcc2.c: TEN live width kills (of twelve guards -- #119 already fixed two in this same file, and its shape is the answer) — commits: b78bb0f — witness: probe:regress/pcc2_width_witness.py -- rung 3, 4/10 on the committed build (three aligned accesses each exit1, four controls green); artifacts/pcc2widthkills/witness_20260903_PREFIX.out — note: *** PASS 2 FOUND SIX CLEAN SWEEPS of the shipped 60-row detector (b78bb0f), the smallest ONE CHARACTER; the REPAIR is on disk, uncommitted: 82 rows (+8 IPL/MASK, +7 per-arm channels, +2 latch cardinality, +1 operand-swap, +4 odd-arm fall-through). Measured: part 1 nine mutants all killed at 78 (part1/driver.log); the builder&#x27;s pass 3 killed all six sweeps at 78 and its 3b showed four fall-through TOTAL SWEEPS at 78 that its 3c kills 81/82 each at 82 (opus_pass3_20260903/); part 2 (M_IDATA_GENCTL vs 82) pending at the time of this note. PRETABLE.out written before table 2 (Section 0 records that table 1 had none). OWED before commit: part 2&#x27;s sentinel, propagate dev_pcc2.c to build/ build-asan/ gxsec-build + two-part clearance, gate 14, CHANGELOG block from the logs, then PASS 3 (the eight other seats; the builder&#x27;s pass 3 is one seat of it).  *** Superseded text, kept: FIXED (uncommitted at the time of writing; commit follows). Twelve width-guard blocks -&gt; direction split: reads ACCEPT (the memcpy above the switch already served them; the tree&#x27;s own header says wide access is LEGAL), writes DECLINE + per-instance 12-bit latch. DELETE is measurably wrong (big-endian compose: the low byte is the neighbour&#x27;s lane) -- M_DELETE killed. The seven odd arms are OPERATOR-reachable (debugger put h, MEASURED) -- all twelve converted, M_OPKILL killed through that path. Detector 60 rows, gate 14 626/0, PREFIX 14/60, BASE 60/60, seven mutants zero sweeps. Design pass on 6 of 9 + one measurement (Opus x2 529, grok x2 CLI). Filed: pcc2c040kill (HIGH), pcc2counter8 (MED), pcc2widecompose. Owes pass 2.  2026-09-04 FIX REVIEW (owner directive): GPT-6 Astra (max) APPROVES the fix, DOES NOT CLOSE; Fable 5.1 GO-WITH-CHANGES.  Seven Astra findings confirmed from the tree; the main loop graded two as open floor cells -- the five HUH?-clear arms were then MEASURED HELD by announce-count rows (part 13 M_HUHV 249/251; the rbq rows strengthen the channel, L4 + coverage, not L2), the INT-set/count-0 cell awaits M_ZINT -&gt; PASS 13 owed: 9 rows (242 -&gt; 251), 7 mutants, gate, panel.  Astra dissents on the floor bound (Opus strength-t); the adjudicator adopts Fable&#x27;s floor + the generating set.  PASS 13 PANEL COMPLETE 9/9 (2026-09-05 02:17-03:46).  RULING: PASS 14 OWED -- the class closure (three file-reading seats derived the same two gaps: the generating set one-sided at the two new INT cells; the INT axis not crossed with the other count), graded L1 (uncommitted detector material).  The pass-13 state is COMMITTED with the obligation OPEN (thirteen uncommitted passes were the larger exposure); pass 14 is drafted (fix_pcc2_p15.py: +18 rows -&gt; 269, 8 mutants, PRETABLE_pass14, plus a pre-repair breach witness part14pre) and runs after the pcc2defaultkill fix ships (owner priority: critical first).
