 VISIBLE REASON; M88K, so the FAULT member is available</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-10-09 — CONFIRMED — VERDICT: MEASURED.  Rung 3, unmodified -E mvme88k -e mvme187, three binaries from git archive 200671b6: HEAD; FAULT (the default: arm&#x27;s exit(1) -&gt; return 0); DECLINE (-&gt; odata = 0; break).  HEAD: rc 1 at all seven sites (MASTERCTL r/w, MASTER3, MASTER4, MASTER4MOD, IRQSTAT, IRQCLR).  FAULT: PC 0x18 (vector 3, VBR 0), DMT0 0x413d (reads) / 0x403f (writes), DMA0 the register address; data CMMU PFSR = PFAR = 0 through a guest ld.  DECLINE: reads 0, writes dropped, PC 0x10008, liveness 0x1234.  Controls green in every binary (T1CMP round-trip, liveness, unassemble).  FLAG (agy): m88k_exception updates the 88100 data-unit registers but never the 88200 CMMU, so a guest fault handler reading PFSR sees SUCCESS. — evidence: regress/artifacts/vmedefaultkill/measure_20261009/agy_vme1009.txt; regress/artifacts/vmedefaultkill/measure_20261009/run_HEAD.out; regress/artifacts/vmedefaultkill/measure_20261009/run_FAULT.out; regress/artifacts/vmedefaultkill/measure_20261009/run_DECLINE.out</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·