ss="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-10-09 — CONFIRMED — VERDICT: WITNESSED.  Rung-3 witness on committed HEAD 200671b6 (binary from git archive, cpu_ppc_instr.c md5 87a766e0), unmodified -E bareppc -M 64: rlwinm. r4,r3,1,31,0 -&gt; r4 0x0, CR 0x20000000 (EQ); rlwinm, rlwnm RB=1 and RB=33 -&gt; 0x0; Book I says 0x0000000200000000 (GT).  Controls: PVR 0x00390000, li liveness, disassembly rlwinm. r4,r3,1,31,0, non-wrapping 0x2.  FLAG (agy): DOT0(rlwinm)&#x27;s update_cr0 then reads the zeroed register, so the condition register is wrong too. — evidence: regress/artifacts/ppcrlwhighhalf/witness_committed_20261009/witness.out; regress/artifacts/ppcrlwhighhalf/witness_committed_20261009/ppc_rlwhigh_witness.py.txt; regress/artifacts/ppcrlwhighhalf/witness_committed_20261009/agy_ppcwit1009.txt</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-26 — MANUAL — GPT-6 Astra, 2026-09-26 -- recorded 2026-10-09 as an UNREAD REVIEW (Fable 5.1&#x27;s 7n-3 found it cited nowhere).  Its section 5 is the rung-3 witness spec the 2026-10-09 witness used (bareppc PPC970; rlwinm. r4,r3,1,31,0 at r3 = 1; predicted HEAD r4 = 0x0 / CR0 EQ vs Book I 0x0000000200000000 / GT; PVR, li-liveness, disassembler and MB=0,ME=31 controls; rlwnm at RB 1 and 33).  Its section 6: the &#x27;dispute unresolved&#x27; title and MED wording are superseded by the 2026-09-10 Book I adjudication; the zero-shift restriction on rlwnm was wrong (every shift is affected); the two base functions are rlwnm then rlwinm. — evidence: regress/artifacts/codexfarm_20260926/codex_ppcrlwhighhalf.txt</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-in work"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">ppcwitnessmaskoracle</span><span class="ttl">harness: the #522 witness&#x27;s rldimi oracle returns ZERO for every wrapping mask and its mask32 omits the high half -- so the two filed sibling rows rest on oracles that cannot certify their own repairs</span><span class="tip">harness: the #522 witness&#x27;s rldimi oracle returns ZERO for every wrapping mask and its mask32 omits the high half -- so the two filed sibling rows rest on oracles that cannot certify their own repairs — commits: a05660af</span></span><span class="state st-in work">in work</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-18 — CONFIRMED — **RATIFY the arithmetic; DISSENT from how the stage was RECORDED and from treating the uncommitted repair as this row&#x27;s discharge.**  Five of seven scriptable verdict lines read DO NOT RATIFY (codex `DO NOT RATIFY AS PRESENTED`, deepseek `DO NOT RATIFY as-is`, minimax `DO NOT RATIFY`, kimi-sub `DO NOT RATIFY YET`, glm `SPLIT, DO NOT RATIFY AS ARCHITECTURE-FINAL`) while **every ledger cell opens `PASS on the UNCOMMITTED oracle repair`** -- a reader takes that as the verdict.  L4: lead each cell with the seat&#x27;s own line.  And codex&#x27;s central finding is ABSENT from its cell, VERIFIED independently: the repaired helpers are called by NO row of `ppc_rldicl_probe.py` -- every `row(...)` calls only `want_rldicl`/`want_rldicr` -- so **the repair cannot change this detector&#x27;s score; it is a repair to DEAD CODE.**  The row&#x27;s real exposure is elsewhere and is already covered (`ppc_rldimi_probe.py` and `ppc_rlwimi_probe.py` carry their own corrected helpers and ARE wired in `gate_ppc.sh`).  What the row still owes is not arithmetic: `ppc_rldicl_probe.py` runs in NO gate under an exemption that **expires 2026-09-20, two days out.** — evidence: _scratchpad/fable_flagship_20260918.md (brief); flagship answer 2026-09-18</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — **KEEP-OPEN -- AND THE BRIEF&#x27;S PREMISE IS REFUTED: THE PROBE IS COMMITTED.**  I wrote *&quot;this file is deliberately NOT committed&quot;*.  `git cat-file -e HEAD:regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py` succeeds -- it shipped in **`e777ff0` (#522)**.  What is uncommitted is the **REPAIR** (`git diff HEAD` = +87/-12).  *** THOSE ARE DIFFERENT CLAIMS, and my phrasing would let a reader conclude no oracle ships at all. *** **It re-derived all three load-bearing numbers from scratch rather than accepting them** -- `rldimi` 2016 of 4096 (MB,SH) pairs give an all-zero old mask (49.2%); `mask_range` all-zero cells over [0,63]^2 = 0; `mask32` identical 528, differ 496, of which differ ONLY in the high 32 bits = 496 -- all matching the docstring exactly.  **And it checked the WARRANT the brief never asked about:** `cpu_ppc_instr.c` computes `rlwinm` wholly in `uint32_t` and assigns to `reg()`, i.e. mask-and-zero-extend -- so the old `mask32` really WAS a copy of the implementation it grades, and *&quot;cannot go red against it&quot;* is true from the source.  The repair is warranted. **WHY IT STAYS OPEN:** the probe is run by **NO GATE**, its exemption expires **2026-09-20**, and its repaired docstring was truncated mid-sentence (L4, repaired 2026-09-17 by MARKING the truncation rather than reconstructing the lost clause). — evidence: _scratchpad/opus_batch5_20260917.md; opus5 answer 2026-09-17</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — MANUAL — PASS on the UNCOMMITTED oracle repair in regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py. Stated its own limit plainly: &#x27;only read-only inspection and in-memory arithmetic checks; no gates, battery, or emulator runs.&#x27;  A READING, not a measurement. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/codex.txt; brief _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/brief_sent.md; _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/SEATS.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — MANUAL — PASS on the UNCOMMITTED oracle repair in regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py. Final verdict GO.  Also flagged an unrelated dated debt: a check_probe_wiring.py exemption expires 2026-09-20. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/agy.txt; brief _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/brief_sent.md; _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/SEATS.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — CONFIRMED — PASS on the UNCOMMITTED oracle repair in regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py. *** UPHELD THE REPAIR AND REFUTED ITS STATED WARRANT. ***  VERDICT: &#x27;the incapable-of-red claim is TRUE of the old mask32 against shipped X(rlwinm) and against ppcrlwhighhalf; the replacement is Book I&#x27;s MASK and can go red on that defect.  Do not treat 131072 as a binary measurement.&#x27;  VERIFIED HERE: ENUMERATION_20260911.txt contains ZERO occurrences of 131072 and says at :49 &#x27;it is a MODEL enumeration, not an emulator measurement.  No binary was built&#x27;.  So the probe&#x27;s word &#x27;Measured&#x27; was a WRONG RECORD of the score-claim class -- a number in a measured column that no run produced.  L4 CORRECTED IN PLACE the same hour.  *** AND THE REPLACEMENT WARRANT IS STRONGER THAN THE NUMBER WAS: the old mask32 IS the shipped handler&#x27;s mask-and-zero-extend, so it agrees BY CONSTRUCTION for every source, not merely across 2^17 encodings -- an oracle that is a copy of the implementation it grades cannot go red against it. ***  grok also derived 47616 = 496x32x3 as the wrapping-encoding figure and warned against claiming this file carries the other three rows&#x27; verdicts. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/grok.txt; brief _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/brief_sent.md; _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/SEATS.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — MANUAL — PASS on the UNCOMMITTED oracle repair in regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py. Reached the right shape independently: &#x27;four ledger rows then need re-measurement on wrapping cells, and ppcrldiclzero may stay closed.&#x27;  The hedge is the accurate part -- ppcrldiclzero DOES stay closed, for the reason minimax missed. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/ollama_kimi.txt; brief _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/brief_sent.md; _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/SEATS.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — MANUAL — PASS on the UNCOMMITTED oracle repair in regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py. Noted the new asserts are dead but harmless -- the b &lt;= e branch is nonempty and the union branch is always nonempty, so the :4031 &#x27;no all-zero mask&#x27; assert can never fire.  A real observation about the repair&#x27;s own defensive code. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/ollama_glm.txt; brief _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/brief_sent.md; _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/SEATS.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — MANUAL — PASS on the UNCOMMITTED oracle repair in regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py. Declined to predict verdict changes for the dependent rows without running the detectors, which the brief forbade.  An honest NOT-CHECKABLE rather than a guess. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/ollama_deepseek.txt; brief _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/brief_sent.md; _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/SEATS.txt</span></span></td><td class="c pend"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">…</span><span class="tip">2026-09-17 — UNKNOWN — PASS on the UNCOMMITTED oracle repair in regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py. *** THE PANEL&#x27;S MOST DRAMATIC FINDING, AND IT IS WRONG.  IT CONFLATES TWO INSTRUCTIONS. ***  minimax claimed want_rldicl is itself a broken oracle because &#x27;rldicl&#x27;s architectural mask is MASK(MB, 63-SH)&#x27; while the code uses mask_b_63(mb) = MASK(mb, 63) -- and concluded ppcrldiclzero&#x27;s CLOSURE &#x27;does not survive a working oracle&#x27;.  REFUTED against the LOCAL Book I (_scratchpad/ppc_uisa_book1_v201.txt): :4064, in the rldicl/rldicr block, gives rldicl m &lt;- MASK(b, 63) -- exactly what mask_b_63 implements.  MASK(b, not-n) at :4129 belongs to **rldic**, a DIFFERENT INSTRUCTION.  Cross-checked by SEMANTICS and not merely by column position, because that manual renders rldicl/rldicr two-up and this project has been bitten by extracted-table stagger: rldicl CLEARS LEFT so it keeps b..63 = MASK(b,63); rldicr CLEARS RIGHT so it keeps 0..e; rldic clears the high b bits THEN shifts left n, which is where 63-SH comes from.  **ppcrldiclzero&#x27;s closure stands.**  Recorded rather than discarded because the seat reasoned correctly from a false premise, and a packet-fed seat could not open Book I to check it. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/ollama_minimax.txt; brief _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/brief_sent.md; _scratchpad/panel_20260917_110605/SEATS.txt</span></span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">ppccr0modewidth</span><span class="ttl">cpu_ppc.c update_cr0(): the comparison width is chosen from the CPU MODEL width (cpu-&gt;cd.ppc.bits) rather than from the current operating mode, so a 64-bit CPU running with SF=0 records 64-bit condition bits</span><span class="tip">cpu_ppc.c update_cr0(): the comparison width is chosen from the CPU MODEL width (cpu-&gt;cd.ppc.bits) rather than from the current operating mode, so a 64-bit CPU running with SF=0 records 64-bit condition bits — note: [2026-10-02] RE-GRADED low -&gt; MED by #554 from the Astra review campaign (retro, DISPOSITIONS.md:163-164; the files are under regress/artifacts/astraretro_20260926/ and astraretro_harness_20260926/).  </span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><