dex="0"><span class="rid">fbirqsoftunimpl</span><span class="ttl">dev_footbridge.c: IRQSoft/FIQSoft (+0x190/+0x290) -- documented WRITE registers (7.3.34, dc21285.txt:6952-6962: a write generates RawStatus bit [1]) with NO case: every legal write announces through default: UNLATCHED and stores nothing.  Member 7, ~8 lines (one case; set/clear irq_status bit 1; reassert); the two addresses are aliases for a SHARED raw bit, not independent pending bits (codex q2 census).  Witness: write +0x190, read +0x184 bit 1 -- the ONLY guest-controllable route to a nonzero irq_status under single-step, which turns #545&#x27;s clause-(e) disclosure into a guest row later.  Own row, not a fiqenableread facet (IRQ-side and live); the next EASY item (fable5 Q5).  Opus seat s12_sibling.out; codex q2.</span><span class="tip">dev_footbridge.c: IRQSoft/FIQSoft (+0x190/+0x290) -- documented WRITE registers (7.3.34, dc21285.txt:6952-6962: a write generates RawStatus bit [1]) with NO case: every legal write announces through default: UNLATCHED and stores nothing.  Member 7, ~8 lines (one case; set/clear irq_status bit 1; reassert); the two addresses are aliases for a SHARED raw bit, not independent pending bits (codex q2 census).  Witness: write +0x190, read +0x184 bit 1 -- the ONLY guest-controllable route to a nonzero irq_status under single-step, which turns #545&#x27;s clause-(e) disclosure into a guest row later.  Own row, not a fiqenableread facet (IRQ-side and live); the next EASY item (fable5 Q5).  Opus seat s12_sibling.out; codex q2.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-19 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) from #545&#x27;s review passes (pass 1 through repair 3e&#x27;s) -- see the row title for the finding, its seat and its evidence.</span><