 colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">fbirqstuck</span><span class="ttl">dev_footbridge.c: the CPU interrupt line can STICK HIGH while IRQ_STATUS reads 0.  footbridge_interrupt_deassert() lowers d-&gt;irq only when d-&gt;irq_asserted is set, and the IRQEnableSet / IRQEnableClear write arms call INTERRUPT_ASSERT(d-&gt;irq) without setting it.  Sequence (Opus seat, #545 repair pass 2, measured in its in-process differential -- regress/artifacts/fbd5/q2_20260923/p2r_20260923/opus_q2r/dom_witness.txt &#x27;model check&#x27;): a device line (cats ISA, line 10) asserts while its enable bit is clear, the guest sets the enable (W188 0x400 -&gt; ASSERT, irq_asserted still 0), the line deasserts -&gt; no DEASSERT; the CPU line stays 1 with nothing pending.  Pre-existing (the enable arms&#x27; bodies are upstream).  Fix: the enable arms maintain irq_asserted exactly as the assert/deassert callbacks do.  Witness owed: rung 3 on -E cats needs a real device line; the offline differential can row it now (it counts the calls).  AND THE PRODUCER PAIR&#x27;S OWN BIT LOGIC IS FILED HERE BY OWNER RULING (2026-09-23), a DIFFERENT defect from the stuck line (grok, #545 3c&#x27;s pass), so the round taking this row owes both: #545&#x27;s detector calls footbridge_interrupt_assert() only to raise one line from an empty status and never calls _deassert(), so `|=` -&gt; `=` in the assert (PR01), the enable test weakened (PR03) and the `~` deleted from _deassert&#x27;s `irq_status &amp;= ~interrupt-&gt;line` (PR04) pass all 864 rows -- disclosed in its contract.  Ready rows: the Opus seat&#x27;s q2e scratch Y8-Y12 (regress/artifacts/fbd5/q2_20260923/q2e_opus/).</span><span class="tip">dev_footbridge.c: the CPU interrupt line can STICK HIGH while IRQ_STATUS reads 0.  footbridge_interrupt_deassert() lowers d-&gt;irq only when d-&gt;irq_asserted is set, and the IRQEnableSet / IRQEnableClear write arms call INTERRUPT_ASSERT(d-&gt;irq) without setting it.  Sequence (Opus seat, #545 repair pass 2, measured in its in-process differential -- regress/artifacts/fbd5/q2_20260923/p2r_20260923/opus_q2r/dom_witness.txt &#x27;model check&#x27;): a device line (cats ISA, line 10) asserts while its enable bit is clear, the guest sets the enable (W188 0x400 -&gt; ASSERT, irq_asserted still 0), the line deasserts -&gt; no DEASSERT; the CPU line stays 1 with nothing pending.  Pre-existing (the enable arms&#x27; bodies are upstream).  Fix: the enable arms maintain irq_asserted exactly as the assert/deassert callbacks do.  Witness owed: rung 3 on -E cats needs a real device line; the offline differential can row it now (it counts the calls).  AND THE PRODUCER PAIR&#x27;S OWN BIT LOGIC IS FILED HERE BY OWNER RULING (2026-09-23), a DIFFERENT defect from the stuck line (grok, #545 3c&#x27;s pass), so the round taking this row owes both: #545&#x27;s detector calls footbridge_interrupt_assert() only to raise one line from an empty status and never calls _deassert(), so `|=` -&gt; `=` in the assert (PR01), the enable test weakened (PR03) and the `~` deleted from _deassert&#x27;s `irq_status &amp;= ~interrupt-&gt;line` (PR04) pass all 864 rows -- disclosed in its contract.  Ready rows: the Opus seat&#x27;s q2e scratch Y8-Y12 (regress/artifacts/fbd5/q2_20260923/q2e_opus/).</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-23 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) from #545&#x27;s review passes (pass 1 through repair 3e&#x27;s) -- see the row title for the finding, its seat and its evidence.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"