tinct at 864 rows: P 78, X1-X8 440, X6 248, X7 148, X8 6, X9 100, X10 72, X11 80, X12 20, X13 20, X14 21), not by WHICH names -- a required row replaced by another uniquely-named passing assertion keeps every count, so a detector edit that swaps a scenario out is invisible to the gate.  Found by the dedicated codex reading on #545&#x27;s first repair (task 4).  Not a floor question for #545 (an edit to the detector, not to the product).  Fix shape: pin a digest of the sorted green-name list per family.  And the gate&#x27;s own footbridge &#x27;Not covered&#x27; summary lists less than the detector&#x27;s NOT COVERED contract (the Opus seat, #545 3d&#x27;s pass, T11) -- a records fix for the same commit that fixes this.</span><span class="tip">gate_offline.sh pins the #545 footbridge families by the COUNT of distinct green row names (fb_distinct at 864 rows: P 78, X1-X8 440, X6 248, X7 148, X8 6, X9 100, X10 72, X11 80, X12 20, X13 20, X14 21), not by WHICH names -- a required row replaced by another uniquely-named passing assertion keeps every count, so a detector edit that swaps a scenario out is invisible to the gate.  Found by the dedicated codex reading on #545&#x27;s first repair (task 4).  Not a floor question for #545 (an edit to the detector, not to the product).  Fix shape: pin a digest of the sorted green-name list per family.  And the gate&#x27;s own footbridge &#x27;Not covered&#x27; summary lists less than the detector&#x27;s NOT COVERED contract (the Opus seat, #545 3d&#x27;s pass, T11) -- a records fix for the same commit that fixes this.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-19 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) from #545&#x27;s review passes (pass 1 through repair 3e&#x27;s) -- see the row title for the finding, its seat and its evidence.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">fbenablewidth</span><span class="ttl">dev_footbridge.c: #545&#x27;s floor ends at the five decline arms; the IRQ/FIQ enable arms (+0x188/+0x288) share no case with a decline, so a `len == 4` conjunct on their direction tests, on the write-data fetch with the Clear address exempted, or `len != 8` on the fetch, passes all 864 rows (measured, regress/artifacts/fbd5/q2_20260923/closing_20260923/CL.log), and IRQEnable&#x27;s 8-byte read (an LDRD at +0x188) is read by no row.  An LDRD/STRD at +0x188 or +0x288 -- or at +0x18c/+0x28c, which the ARM load/store unit aligns down onto them -- is a guest input.  Disclosed in the contract.  Fix shape: X9/X10 rows for the enable arms at width 8 and the narrow Set/FIQ writes, each with a measured variant.</span><span class="tip">dev_footbridge.c: #545&#x27;s floor ends at the five decline arms; the IRQ/FIQ enable arms (+0x188/+0x288) share no case with a decline, so a `len == 4` conjunct on their direction tests, on the write-data fetch with the Clear address exempted, or `len != 8` on the fetch, passes all 864 rows (measured, regress/artifacts/fbd5/q2_20260923/closing_20260923/CL.log), and IRQEnable&#x27;s 8-byte read (an LDRD at +0x188) is read by no row.  An LDRD/STRD at +0x188 or +0x288 -- or at +0x18c/+0x28c, which the ARM load/store unit aligns down onto them -- is a guest input.  Disclosed in the contract.  Fix shape: X9/X10 rows for the enable arms at width 8 and the narrow Set/FIQ writes, each with a measured variant.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-23 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) from #545&#x27;s review passes (pass 1 through repair 3e&#x27;s) -- see the