d there because the text is the timer campaign&#x27;s: &#x27;EVERY REAL ROW IN THIS FILE COMPARES NUMBERS&#x27; (E2, E3, F1 and G1 compare strings); the fbclearread paragraph in the present tense (&#x27;case TIMER_1_CLEAR: carries NO writeflag test&#x27;) after #474 guarded it; and &#x27;a DISABLED timer can never hold a pending interrupt&#x27; (also in gate_offline.sh) -- the timer callbacks count pending ticks without testing TIMER_ENABLE, and disabling does not remove the registered timer: a product question for the timer campaign as well as a records one.</span><span class="tip">records: three pre-existing false sentences in regress/diff_footbridge.c and regress/gate_offline.sh, filed from #545&#x27;s passes rather than edited there because the text is the timer campaign&#x27;s: &#x27;EVERY REAL ROW IN THIS FILE COMPARES NUMBERS&#x27; (E2, E3, F1 and G1 compare strings); the fbclearread paragraph in the present tense (&#x27;case TIMER_1_CLEAR: carries NO writeflag test&#x27;) after #474 guarded it; and &#x27;a DISABLED timer can never hold a pending interrupt&#x27; (also in gate_offline.sh) -- the timer callbacks count pending ticks without testing TIMER_ENABLE, and disabling does not remove the registered timer: a product question for the timer campaign as well as a records one.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-23 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) from #545&#x27;s review passes (pass 1 through repair 3e&#x27;s) -- see the row title for the finding, its seat and its evidence.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">fbbufbounds</span><span class="ttl">regress/diff_footbridge.c: the footbridge handler&#x27;s use of the caller&#x27;s buffer beyond `len` is checked only after X6&#x27;s declined accesses and X9/X10&#x27;s legal reads (#545 3e&#x27;s pad_kept).  A real ARM narrow load or store hands the device a 1-, 2- or 4-byte buffer (cpu_arm_instr_loadstore.c).  Unobserved on the 864 rows: (1) a FETCH past len whose value no channel uses -- every declined write, and the Opus seat&#x27;s FW03 (an 8-byte fetch at len 4, measured green, equivalent for the guest) -- UNOBSERVABLE here by construction (the harness&#x27;s memory helpers record no length); (2) a STORE past len inside a legal write -- `data[len] = 0` in the Clear write (codex, 3e&#x27;s pass; measured green, qwb QDLEN); (3) the common tail&#x27;s write-back past len at the legal reads outside X9/X10&#x27;s five registers, among them VENDOR_ID (+0x00), the timer value (+0x304; +0x324/+0x344/+0x364 fold onto it), FIQEnable (+0x288) and the FIQEnableClear read (+0x28c) -- which X7 reads, and X3 three of them, unchecked -- and the timer LOAD and CLEAR reads, whose 4-byte harness buffer an 8-byte write-back overflows SILENTLY: an 8-byte write-back keyed on any of the seven passes every row (measured, regress/artifacts/fbd5/q2_20260923/qwb_20260923/, three runs, predictions first -- ORDER_NOTE.txt names the file proving each run&#x27;s order).  Above #545&#x27;s floor (the tail and the fetch are not predicates dominating the edited arms): disclosed in the contract by repair 3f and filed; the flagship seat&#x27;s final adjudication upheld the filing.  Fix shape: pad_kept after every read in X3, X7 and the timer rows and after each narrow write in X12/X13 (a new channel on rows that exist, so it owes a table), and a length-recording memory helper for the fetch.</span><span class="tip">regress/diff_footbridge.c: the footbridge handler&#x27;s use of the caller&#x27;s buffer beyond `len` is checked only after X6&#x27;s declined accesses and X9/X10&#x27;s legal reads (#545 3e&#x27;s pad_kept).  A real ARM narrow load or store hands the device a 1-, 2- or 4-byte buffer (cpu_arm_instr_loadstore.c).  Unobserved on the 864 rows: (1) a FETCH past len whose value no channel uses -- every declined write, and the Opus seat&#x27;s FW03 (an 8-byte fetch at len 4, measured green, equivalent for the guest) -- UNOBSERVABLE here by construction (the harness&#x27;s memory helpers record no length); (2) a STORE past len inside a legal write -- `data[len] = 0` in the Clear write (codex, 3e&#x27;s pass; measured green, qwb QDLEN); (3) the common tail&#x27;s write-back past len at the legal reads outside X9/X10&#x27;s five registers, among them VENDOR_ID (+0x00), the timer value (+0x304; +0x324/+0x344/+0x364 fold onto it), FIQEnable (+0x288) and the FIQEnableClear read (+0x28c) -- which X7 reads, and X3 three of them, unchecked -- and the timer LOAD and CLEAR reads, whose 4-byte harness buffer an 8-byte write-back overflows SILENTLY: an 8-byte write-back keyed on any of the seven passes every row (measured, regress/artifacts/fbd5/q2_20260923/qwb_20260923/, three runs, predictions first -- ORDER_NOTE.txt names the file proving each run&#x27;s order).  Above #545&#x27;s floor (the tail and the fetch are not predicates dominating the edited arms): disclosed in the contract by repair 3f and filed; the flagship seat&#x27;s final adjudication upheld the filing.  Fix shape: pad_kept after every read in X3, X7 and the timer rows and after each narrow write in X12/X13 (a new channel on rows that exist, so it owes a table), and a length-recording memory helper for the fetch.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-23 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) from #545&#x27;s review passes (pass 1 through repair 3e&#x27;s) -- see the row title for the finding, its seat and its evidence.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">hygienecensusholes</span><span class="ttl">gate_hygiene.sh&#x27;s readiness census is a SPELLING census.  The census round (#546, pass 2 -&gt; F6e) rebuilt its POSITIVE classifications on Python tokens (regress/census_tokens.py: a comment, a string or a docstring is not code; statement boundaries kept; per-occurrence counts), which closed the comment / string / docstring and most spacing evasions pass 2 and F2 measured.  STILL OPEN, each measured passing all 12 readiness rows on the shipped F6e (regress/artifacts/hygienecensus_20260923/controls_c6e/TABLE.txt, the F2 suite): e9, RANKED FIRST -- the TEXTUAL counts are LINE-based and key on `endswith(`, so a space before the paren (`buf.endswith (&quot;&gt;&quot;)`, the #37 bare defect behind one space) or a backslash continuation (t_bsl) removes a call from all of them; another receiver name (e_e1, n3h); `strip()` or `rstrip(&quot;\r\n&quot;)` for `rstrip()` (e_e5, n3f); a slice compare (e_e4; n10, `buf.rstrip()[-1:] == &quot;&gt;&quot;`, the bare defect again); a parenthesised receiver (n3b, n3c); a regex readiness test (n3i); readiness moved into a helper module (n3k, n3k2 -- no count sees WHICH probe a helper serves); a probe forking with `forkpty` (n4a -- outside the pty census entirely); `~` on the call (t_tilde, the lexical limit); e10 -- the comment filter drops every PHYSICAL line beginning with `#`, so code after a closing triple quote or in an f-string field, or a whole file saved with CR-only line endings, escapes (the census F4 pass, the Opus seat).  And the deriver&#x27;s writers are not ATOMIC: a write that fails part-way (a full disk) leaves the gate truncated -- reported since F6e as DERIVE_FAIL rc 6 (controls_c6e t_dfwrite, t_dfgrand); a temporary beside the gate and a rename would keep the old one.  Ranked below live defects: the census guards spellings, not readiness.</span><span class="tip">gate_hygiene.sh&#x27;s readiness census is a SPELLING census.  The census round (#546, pass 2 -&gt; F6e) rebuilt its POSITIVE classifications on Python tokens (regress/census_tokens.py: a comment, a string or a docstring is not code; statement boundaries kept; per-occurrence counts), which closed the comment / string / docstring and most spacing evasions pass 2 and F2 measured.  STILL OPEN, each measured passing all 12 readiness rows on the shipped F6e (regress/artifacts/hygienecensus_20260923/controls_c6e/TABLE.txt, the F2 suite): e9, RANKED FIRST -- the TEXTUAL counts are LINE-based and key on `endswith(`, so a space before the paren (`buf.endswith (&quot;&gt;&quot;)`, the #37 bare defect behind one space) or a backslash continuation (t_bsl) removes a call from all of them; another receiver name (e_e1, n3h); `strip()` or `rstrip(&quot;\r\n&quot;)` for `rstrip()` (e_e5, n3f); a slice compare (e_e4; n10, `buf.rstrip()[-1:] == &quot;&gt;&quot;`, the bare defect again); a parenthesised receiver (n3b, n3c); a regex readiness test (n3i); readiness moved into a helper module (n3k, n3k2 -- no count sees WHICH probe a helper serves); a probe forking with `forkpty` (n4a -- outside the pty census entirely); `~` on the call (t_tilde, the lexical limit); e10 -- the comment filter drops every PHYSICAL line beginning with `#`, so code after a closing triple quote or in an f-string field, or a whole file saved with CR-only line endings, escapes (the census F4 pass, the Opus seat).  And the deriver&#x27;s writers are not ATOMIC: a write that fails part-way (a full disk) leaves the gate truncated -- reported since F6e as DERIVE_FAIL rc 6 (controls_c6e t_dfwrite, t_dfgrand); a temporary beside the gate and a rename would keep the old one.  Ranked below live defects: the census guards spellings, not readiness.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-09-23 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) from the census round&#x27;s review passes (pass 2 through F6e&#x27;s controls) -- see the row title for each finding, its seat and its evidence.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class=