sting</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">qhmbphasestops</span><span class="ttl">An MB89352 data-register access, with a transfer object and a nonzero count, in a phase unsupported for the access direction stops the emulated CPU</span><span class="tip">An MB89352 data-register access, with a transfer object and a nonzero count, in a phase unsupported for the access direction stops the emulated CPU — note: FILED BY #558 from queue passage 2616 at db8b1a33 (&#x27;#12 m88k CMMU / dev_mb89352 fatal errors&#x27;), which #555 gave ONE row (qhm88kstops, dev_mb89352.c:146).  SITES (c29a5fd3, src/devices/dev_mb89352.c): :169 (DREG read, phase outside DATAIN/STAT/MSGIN) and :235 (DREG write, phase outside DATAOUT/CMD).  :290 (the end-of-write default:) is UNREACHABLE: the first switch returns only for unsupported phases, and DATAOUT/CMD break, reach the second switch with no intervening phase change, and exhaust its supported cases.  PREREQUISITES: every DREG helper call needs a NONZERO count before decrement (a zero-count access only warns) and these guards additionally need a transfer object -- &#x27;unconditional&#x27; means independent of the abort flag, nothing more.  REACHED BY (by reading, not measured): SCMD/PCTL give the guest control of the phase.  FIX SHAPE: keep the CPU running while KEEPING the helper&#x27;s early return (:170 / :236) -- the treatment #186 gave the XFR command at :507.  PROVENANCE: agy&#x27;s ifiled2_1 flag #27 (PARTLY) -&gt; GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s finding that the title carries one of nine `cpu-&gt;running = 0` assignments (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/aconf_agyflags/codex_aconf_agyflags.txt) -&gt; grok&#x27;s ruling, CONCEDE IN PART, three rows (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/grok/grok_mbstops.txt) -&gt; Astra&#x27;s confirmation (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/aconf_mbstops/codex_aconf_mbstops.txt: CONFIRMED WITH CHANGES (3) -- correct reachability explanations, qualify carrier/title scope, and label evidence as source-only; retain three HIGH rows).  Severity HIGH by the qhm88kstops grade (a guest-drivable stop of the emulated CPU).  Reachability established by source inspection at c29a5fd3; no runtime witness measured -- the round that takes this row owes the rung-3 attempt.  NOT FIXED by #558.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-10-02 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) by #558 on grok&#x27;s ruling (grok-4.7 xhigh, plan mode) and Astra&#x27;s confirmation of it (GPT-6 Astra, ultra); the chain is in the row&#x27;s note.  NOT FIXED by #558.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span 