 :312 (len != 1: a halfword or word callback access), :533 (an SCMD WRITE outside {0x00, 0x20, 0x84, 0x8c, 0xc0} unless bit 0x10 rewrites it to BUS_REL -- an SCMD read does not execute this switch), and EXBF, register index 15: WRITE logging at :676 and READ logging at :683 converge on the ONE assignment at :690.  All gated by const bool mb89352_abort_on_unimplemented_stuff = true (:61), so live; the shared fixed-true policy is what groups them.  REACHED BY (by reading, not measured): those accesses from the guest&#x27;s register interface.  FIX SHAPE: the warning branch the flag already selects; clearing the flag leaves all five live unconditional DREG assignments (:146, :169, :176, :235, :242; :290 is dead) intact.  NOT mb89352halt&#x27;s stop: that dropped row&#x27;s record names the disk dispatcher&#x27;s CDB default: and the controller&#x27;s status-length guard, not :533.  PROVENANCE: agy&#x27;s ifiled2_1 flag #27 (PARTLY) -&gt; GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s finding that the title carries one of nine `cpu-&gt;running = 0` assignments (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/aconf_agyflags/codex_aconf_agyflags.txt) -&gt; grok&#x27;s ruling, CONCEDE IN PART, three rows (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/grok/grok_mbstops.txt) -&gt; Astra&#x27;s confirmation (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/aconf_mbstops/codex_aconf_mbstops.txt: CONFIRMED WITH CHANGES (3) -- correct reachability explanations, qualify carrier/title scope, and label evidence as source-only; retain three HIGH rows).  Severity HIGH by the qhm88kstops grade (a guest-drivable stop of the emulated CPU).  Reachability established by source inspection at c29a5fd3; no runtime witness measured -- the round that takes this row owes the rung-3 attempt.  NOT FIXED by #558.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span clas