><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">qhmbbufendstops</span><span class="ttl">An MB89352 data-register access at or past the end of the selected buffer, in a phase supported for the access direction, stops the emulated CPU</span><span class="tip">An MB89352 data-register access at or past the end of the selected buffer, in a phase supported for the access direction, stops the emulated CPU — note: FILED BY #558 from queue passage 2616 at db8b1a33 (&#x27;#12 m88k CMMU / dev_mb89352 fatal errors&#x27;), which #555 gave ONE row (qhm88kstops, dev_mb89352.c:146).  SITES (c29a5fd3, src/devices/dev_mb89352.c): :176 (DREG read, transfer_bufpos &gt;= len against the selected DATAIN, STAT or MSGIN buffer -- read completion changes phase WITHOUT resetting the cursor, so a subsequent nonempty buffer can meet this guard, not only the original DATAIN buffer) and :242 (DREG write: reachable through empty or unprepared outgoing-buffer states; an exact fill runs completion and can change phase so a further write reaches :235 instead).  PREREQUISITES: a transfer object and a nonzero count, as for the phase guards (the count prerequisite applies to every DREG helper call; the :146 stop is the case with NO transfer object).  CARRIERS OF THE REST: b120 carries the unknown-CDB producer omission and its empty-status consequence; this row&#x27;s residual is every OTHER empty-buffer path and every nonempty-buffer case.  FIX SHAPE: keep the bounds protection and refuse the access or handle phase completion -- removing the guard exposes the indexed accesses at :180 / :246 -- a CONTROLLER fix; b120 remains the PRODUCER fix.  PROVENANCE: agy&#x27;s ifiled2_1 flag #27 (PARTLY) -&gt; GPT-6 Astra&#x2