ls; 2 left empty on purpose (asanunbuildable, wiringshghost); boilerplateprefix&#x27;s filled by the post step with #557&#x27;s own sha; 14 nothing owed; 5 work still alive -- 4 added as members below, the fifth, boilerplateprefix, landed by #557 itself.  boilerplateprefix and smhang are in both the shipped twenty and the alive five, which is why those three counts sum past 37.  FILLING THE FIELDS BROUGHT THE ROWS UNDER SECTIONS K AND I FOR THE FIRST TIME (the 19:10 precheck): 3 witness fields added and 2 re-shaped, 8 regress reviews held with their questions -- K&#x27;s witness-presence rule and I&#x27;s missing-regress rule both key on the commits field, so a closed-with-no-commit row escapes exactly those two (the same precheck also found #556&#x27;s hrecordowed unattributed, section L, a separate leftover).  MEMBERS NOW (12): m8latch, gcsections, ns16550, pcchalt, wdcstandby, rtcnarrow, scunbacked, m437multi, cmtattr, gdromcontractresidual, smhang, unreadseats23.  A CLASS ROW (a records defect of the ledger).  MEMBERS (8): m8latch, gcsections, ns16550, pcchalt, wdcstandby, rtcnarrow, scunbacked, m437multi.  READ BY NO SEAT (2), closed by the same sweep with no commit: ledgerwitness, cmtattr.  Nothing is re-opened by this row: the audit of each member -- re-open, re-file, or close with a commit -- is its work.  The ruling seat&#x27;s evidence (grok/grok_grok_irule_d.txt 5 (conceding in part; Astra&#x27;s ifile_04 raised it)): `CLOSE (assess)` signs off the assess stage. The seven rows whose notes continue past it are still live: `i8253zero` held (`ledger.json:9278`), `idesync` in work (`:12953`), `wdcflood` in work (`:13498`), `landiskdisk` in work (`:13993`), `rtcflood` held (`:15096`), `floodclass` held (`:15480`), `isaorder` held (`:16315`). The sweep&#x27;s own text, `ledger.json:10393`, closed the bare note and performed no re-check. Eleven is too many. Checked and still undone, with no later carrier: `m8latch` (`dev_m8820x.c:90-97`), `gcsections` (`gate_offline.sh:729`, `:820`), `ns16550` (`dev_ns16550.c:181`), `pcchalt` (no `regress/ppc*.py` page-crossing probe; halt comment only at `cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c:63-84`), `wdcstandby` (`WDCC_STANDBY_IMMED` is `0xe0` at `wdcreg.h:138` and still hits `default:` with `WDCE_ABRT` at `dev_wdc.c:1155-1156`), `rtcnarrow` (`dev_vr41xx.c:606` integer-divides `RTCL1_L_HZ / idata` and `:614` ignores the high half; `ledger.json:15084` says the core floor is the wrong fix site), `scunbacked` (`gate_offline.sh:2346-2349` still greps bare `@@SELFCHECK@@` while `diff_rtc_range.c:140` names that token in a comment), `m437multi` (`diskimage.c:1291-1292` still writes only the last overlay, and `:2395-2412` fails the sync if any overlay fsync fails). Checked and left out: `m8sarseq` is carried by open `m8sarrows` (`ledger.json:25702-25704`); `xfamscope`&#x27;s two edits are in `gate_crossfamily.sh:173-193` and `:207-218`; `m437rtmp` owes no code, and its scope statement is `OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md:5806-5810` with the `R:` unlink at `diskimage.c:177-182`. One carrier, and this ruling does not re-open the closed rows. Passages 1-3 point here. Passage 4 does not.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-10-02 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) by #555.  GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s closing check of the id-less table (ifile_04, part D) found open work in four queue passages that were pointed only at closed rows; the main loop read the closures and proposed the class; the grok seat ruled it first-hand and cut the members to the ones it found undone.  NOT FIXED by #555.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">idlesslow</span><span class="ttl">CLASS ROW: the 94 LOW rows the id-less review of OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md filed -- prose entries of the queue that now have ids; each is listed with its id in OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md (2026-10-02, #555) and promoted to its own row when a round takes it up</span><span class="tip">CLASS ROW: the 94 LOW rows the id-less review of OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md filed -- prose entries of the queue that now have ids; each is listed with its id in OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md (2026-10-02, #555) and promoted to its own row when a round takes it up — note: MEMBERS (94), id -- title: qharmwbdebt -- Owed record correction of the stale general-load coverage claims, cross-referencing qharmgenstore for the cold general-store row and qharmpathaudit for the measured inventory re-audit || qharmmultiorder -- One order-blind ARM multi emitter, latent behind the little-endian install gate; a future big-endian path must emit endian variants and swap the memcpy fold&#x27;s raw publishes in that same change || qhmutcrashscore -- selftest_mutation.sh treats a mutant that crashes, times out, or prints nothing as detected, because it ignores the exit status and counts DIFF_PASS || qharmpcmeasure -- ARM PC 0xfffff000 case is still unmeasured || qhshapprox -- fsca and fsrra rounding choice is still marked unsourced || qhdiagrest -- Unlatched ASC diagnostics remain owed, and the repaired DEBUG-gated FDC diagnostics leave this debt. || qhvgasizestate -- VGA updates its cached framebuffer size even when resize is rejected || qhnetxlog -- Both queue passages record one defect: an invalid NE2000 transmit span emits an unlatched WARNING, which default INFO verbosity includes. || qhfpguesttest -- Owed committed-record coverage of live c.olt and c.ole remains, with the compiler prerequisite removed. || qhselectretry -- d_avail retries every select error, including errors other than EINTR || qhrunctrlt -- CTRL-T in the run loop is still commented out || qhcuepathlink -- CUE/image open follows a symlink after the lexical .. check || qhatapiwitness -- Landisk ATAPI witness remains owed; offline accounting checks exist || qharmmemsetdead -- netbsd_memset arming is overwritten by the beq_etc catch-all || qhmemsetalias -- latent netbsd_memset overwrites IP with the pre-subs address plus 128 || qhccmcrskip -- cache-clean folds skip MCRs that cr7 currently implements as a no-op || qhmemreadflood -- missing-physical-memory reads log one warning per access || qharmreadaudit -- Owed coverage of ARM read-ahead on the guest path, because these probes install breakpoints and breakpoints disable read-ahead. || qhstrlenbilling -- strlen probe cannot check 3n-1 billing closer than about 8K || qhcpycoldremeas -- cold-source memcpy fold count is unreconciled and still queued for re-measurement || qhcpybailrate -- Owed real-guest measurement of the memcpy bail rate, including silent zero-iteration bails. || qhcpybillmeas -- Owed measurement of whether the -J arm and the marker arms agree on instruction billing. || qhcpytailcov -- memcpy probe has no two-iteration tail row at word 16 || qhcpydumpdiag -- memcpy probe treats a short dump as a bad destination word || qhcpysamplecov -- memcpy probe samples five destination words and misses a 7-of-8 copy || qhbatchcounter -- the guest mp counter includes the dyntrans batch quantum of 120 || qhstepbranch -- Owed observation of a step onto a fold slot reached as a branch target, under the source-derived expectation of uncombined execution. || qhusertlbmeas -- Owed measurement of is_userpage across TLB eviction, recording that invalidation clears the bit. || qhcpycountcov -- memcpy marker-count times 32 is unchecked against the r0 advance || qhfireexact -- copyin and copyout fires rows accept any positive marker count || qharmtucov -- three ARM load/store translation units still have no writeback-probe row || qharmstorepre -- store pre-index writeback has no probe row || qhwalloracles -- Owed assessment of wall-clock measurement oracles and fixed execution windows, including halt-within-window gates, grace constants, and run_emu margins; transport timeouts stay with loadfragile || qharmstaleprompt -- arm_flags_probe whole-buffer waits return on the previous prompt || qharmsendstatus -- arm_flags_probe send drops the prompt-wait result || qharmreadretry -- six register, print, and copyout reads still have no consumer-keyed retry || qharmdumptail -- dump retry parsers take the first dump word in the slice || qharmretrycount -- Report retries and unparseable reads as diagnostic telemetry; do not require zero retries || qharmcolorenv -- gate_arm.sh still does not unset CLICOLOR || qhfpdefaultnote -- float_emul.c still documents the withdrawn R3010/R4010 integer default || qharmgenstore -- arm_writeback_probe.py lacks a cold general-store row || qharmgenwidth -- arm_writeback_probe.py still lacks cold general-path rows for the byte arm, the halfword alignment mask, and register-offset forms. || qharmfasthstore -- the fast store-halfword site has no probe row || qharmpathaudit -- Owed measured re-audit of the ARM translation-unit inventory, correcting four missing units to three and cross-referencing qharmtucov || qhmipsdump -- mips_rounding_probe accepts any dump-shaped line in the read slice || qhmipslong -- arc round.l, ceil.l, and floor.l still have no row || qhfpucomment -- Owed record correction of the comment that W/L stores ignore the rounding mode and that cvt.w and trunc.w are indistinguishable. || qhidlefoldloss -- The m88k idle fold is lost only for loop-head tb1 at page index zero when a .n branch ends the previous page || qhswpabort -- swp abort prints via fatal and returns without the next_ic reset || qhptyfault -- the #391 timeout detector still has no PTY-level fault injection || qhcmdresults -- sibling probe sends still drop the wait verdict || qhcmdecho -- register reads accept a bare hex line with no command echo || qhcmdabort -- A stalled pc=, step, or print is still unacted, so its late output shifts the next bare-hex read into the following register || qhcmdreaderr -- EOF and read errors are reported as timeouts || qhcmdclock -- probe deadlines use time.time || qhctrlcwait -- post-control-C wait_from results are discarded || qhdhighseed -- High-bit LDRD rows already exist, and the owed work is their mutation and sanitizer verification. || qhdwarmrows -- a warm STRD page has no row, so the fast-path chicken-out has no detector || qhdaddrrows -- LDRD and STRD register-offset and writeback rows remain owed, together with the STRD write-extent sentinel. || qhmipscensus -- Complete and record the deferred Phase-C MIPS fold census || bareflopq -- bare floppy-sized image is typed FLOPPY and no device selects that type || parsecovq -- Parser tests do not establish controller acceptance || gateorderq -- Binary withdrawal and republication, and baseline-directory producer-consumer order, still serialize the regression battery. || idlepatq -- The pinned luna88k instruction budget depends on recognizing specific guest idle patterns. || finalcountq -- SIGINT with absent or exhausted stdin blocks in the debugger before any final instruction count, while quit exits cleanly only when a command can be read. || landrateq -- landisk still has no calibrated instruction budget || logspliceq -- bracketed fatal() text can splice a guest console line || anchorevq -- Owed record correction: the anchored-regex result was measured on whole logs and does not describe streaming, which matches each assembled tail at a new position-zero boundary. || tailstepq -- Interactive confirmations ignore held stream tails || landwallq -- landisk&#x27;s runaway bound is still 900 s of wall clock || canaryq -- Gate 5 ordinary rig runs still lack a standing mutant control, and gate 7 synthetic progress controls stay a separate case. || runnamesq -- Gate 5 writes and grades fixed filenames in a reusable log namespace and never checks a run identifier. || armapcovq -- The memory differential ignores real ARM subpage permission selection, grants its 1 KiB fixture access, tests mapping splits, and names both ARM and SH as producers. || qhwdcempty -- no-disk WDC commands print an unlatched debug line per command || shdmacmask -- DMATCR&#x27;s transfer path masks 29 bits while the register write path keeps 24 || shdnrecords -- DN=0 comments still describe an FPU error where the manual specifies a denormal result || shfsrracite -- the FSRRA comment at cpu_sh_instr.c:3281 still says single-precision only || shszpin -- SZ1 is not assigned to bit 7 or bit 4 by either manual and has no empirical pin || shregattribution -- SH7760, CHCR_TD/CHCR_CHSET, and SH_RCR2_ENABLE comments name the wrong chip or the wrong bit || pclockdeadcode -- Owed probe hygiene: sh_pclock_probe.py keeps an unused dumped helper and duplicate landisk and dreamcast code entries. || gdromwideval -- a declined 32-bit GDROM_DATA read returns 0x0000ffff and no row pins it || gdromlatchspent -- Owed documentation, with no code change: the GDROM width warning latch is consumed before the declined store, so a later landing narrow store stays silent. || gdrom88rd -- A read of GDROM 0x88 and a write of GDROM_STAT still call fatal with no latch, and the read is the flood that was ordered filed rather than latched || wdcoddstubclaim -- row_odd_bytecount still says the harness does not stub diskimage_is_a_cdrom || gdrommaskclaim -- Owed correction of the GDROM comment that still promises a new warn site cannot reuse another site&#x27;s bit, a promise the following sentences retract. || seatcopywait -- copy preserved seat logs after the panel wait || panelechocheck -- ECHO-ONLY requires both the distinctive brief line in the answer and answer-minus-brief under 800; the owed work is a harness change plus two negative controls || shfaultclause -- Owed record correction, deferred to carrier review and still owed: the member-5 clause omits that a failed SH load leaves its destination unchanged. || qhmipstlbwarn -- The optional write-time MIPS TLB-overlap debug warning remains compiled out and was left unimplemented; it is tooling, not a fidelity defect || armcpsrprint -- A direct debugger print of cpsr can show stale NZCV because the settings read does not fold the separate execution-flags field back into CPSR || pcc2lineexit -- pcctwo_interrupt_common&#x27;s default still calls exit on an unsupported interrupt line, and guest reachability is unestablished || qhshelltimeout -- gate scripts still bound emulator runs with the timeout command || qhguestasan -- the asan sweep constructs machines under -V and never executes a guest instruction || gdromtailcov -- ship cnt-post tail-reach rows for both GD-ROM rejection arms</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c tok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">∅</span><span class="tip">2026-10-02 — [NOT A SEAT ANSWER] Filed by GXEMUL [087a90] (main loop) by #555 from the id-less review of OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md.  This row closes when every member is promoted, fixed or dropped; the members&#x27; rulings are in regress/artifacts/idless_20261002/IDLESS_DISPOSITIONS.md and regress/artifacts/idless_20261002/IDLESS_TABLE2.tsv.  NOT FIXED by #555.</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><t