</td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">armusrstop</span><span class="ttl">cpu_arm_instr.c: a USER/SYSTEM-mode guest stops the CPU -- LDM {..pc}^ (arm_pop) and MSR SPSR_x (msr_imm_spsr) in USR32/SYS32 reach default: arms that set running = 0 (stops the current CPU; emulation ends when no CPU runs)</span><span class="tip">cpu_arm_instr.c: a USER/SYSTEM-mode guest stops the CPU -- LDM {..pc}^ (arm_pop) and MSR SPSR_x (msr_imm_spsr) in USR32/SYS32 reach default: arms that set running = 0 (stops the current CPU; emulation ends when no CPU runs) — note: filed 2026-10-07 from the Opus 5.5 seat&#x27;s pass-1 answer on armmsrmodekill (F2 disposition 12; owner ruling 2026-10-07: FILE as its own row, not fixed in #562).  USR/SYS have no SPSR, so the architecture makes these UNPREDICTABLE; stopping the CPU is not a permitted outcome (DDI 0100I glossary: must not halt or hang).  Not yet witnessed on HEAD by a rung-3 probe.  Evidence: regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/witness_20261007/opus_pass1.md.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">armspsrthumb</span><span class="ttl">cpu_arm: an SPSR restore (LDM {..pc}^, DPI S-to-PC) that sets T keeps decoding ARM words until the dyntrans run loop is next entered -- the Thumb interpreter is chosen only at loop entry, arm_pop never breaks out and word-aligns the PC</span><span class="tip">cpu_arm: an SPSR restore (LDM {..pc}^, DPI S-to-PC) that sets T keeps decoding ARM words until the dyntrans run loop is next entered -- the Thumb interpreter is chosen only at loop entry, arm_pop never breaks out and word-aligns the PC — note: filed 2026-10-07 by owner ruling, from #562&#x27;s §F2 pass (codex disposition 6: &#x27;Mode filtering alone does not make applying T safe or coherent&#x27;).  CORRECTED 2026-10-08 by reading the source before the round&#x27;s records were written: the first filing said a restored T=1 &#x27;is not honoured&#x27; -- it IS, but late.  cpu_dyntrans.c picks arm_cpu_interpret_thumb_SLOW only at the run function&#x27;s ENTRY (`if (cpu-&gt;cd.arm.cpsr &amp; ARM_FLAG_T)`); the DPI restore breaks out (abortdyntrans_call) only for an ODD destination PC; arm_pop never breaks out and loads the PC as r[ARM_PC] &amp; 0xfffffffc, dropping bit 1 of a Thumb address.  So after a restore that sets T the CPU can keep decoding ARM words until the loop is next entered.  Out of #562&#x27;s scope (#562 declines only M[4:0]; its probe&#x27;s `tbit&#x27; row pins the T BIT&#x27;s provenance, not the decoder).  Not witnessed; the round owes a rung-3 attempt first.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">armmmuvehicle</span><span class="ttl">regress: an ARM rung-3 probe vehicle that runs a guest with the MMU ON (testarm, debugger-driven) -- the reopen condition of armthumbabortkill and the likely vehicle for armdesc3kill / armdacr2kill</span><span class="tip">regress: an ARM rung-3 probe vehicle that runs a guest with the MMU ON (testarm, debugger-driven) -- the reopen condition of armthumbabortkill and the likely vehicle for armdesc3kill / armdacr2kill — note: filed 2026-10-07 by owner ruling: after #562, build this FIRST, then armthumbabortkill.  Open questions: does testarm&#x27;s default CPU (SA1110, ARMv4) support Thumb, or is another -C cpu needed; page-table setup in guest RAM via debugger writes; translation-fault liveness control.  Test-apparatus round (witness kind harness:).  2026-10-08 agy READING (regress/artifacts/armmmuvehicle/agy_research_20261008.txt; facts to re-derive, not agreement): testarm default CPU SA1110; NO per-CPU Thumb capability flag -- the T bit alone selects arm_cpu_interpret_thumb_SLOW, so any -C runs Thumb; CP15 c1/c2/c3 are NOT debugger-settable -&gt; the guest must mcr them; `put&#x27; writes VIRTUAL memory; `step&#x27; keeps working with the MMU on; minimal map = one section descriptor 0x00000c02 at a 16 KB-aligned TTB, DACR 1.  THE VEHICLE MUST MAP THE EXCEPTION VECTORS or a fault reaches cpu_dyntrans.c&#x27;s &#x27;could not find physical address of the exception handler&#x27; exit (tracked as alphaifetchkill).  Of the exits and stops agy listed on this path, these match existing rows by title: armdesc3kill, armdacr2kill, armcp15cp14exits, armendianexit, qharmexalign, alphaifetchkill.  NOT complete, and two entries were wrong as given (GPT-6 Astra, #562&#x27;s confirmation): armsa1110areset is the reset alignment-control default, not the ARM_EXCEPTION_RESET exit agy listed (that exit may be unfiled), and agy&#x27;s &#x27;wfi&#x27; stop in cpu_arm_instr.c is X(reboot).</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">armmsrmodedebt</span><span class="ttl">#562&#x27;s arm_msrmode_probe.py: measured residue -- latch-CLEAR x bits 31:8 at the restores (5 escapes), msr label x latch (2), the cached ic-&gt;arg[] (M_msr_argmask), grid cov asserting G1 only -- with measured closures for the five restore-flag escapes (a session reorder) and the cached-translation mutants (a 48th loop row)</span><span class="tip">#562&#x27;s arm_msrmode_probe.py: measured residue -- latch-CLEAR x bits 31:8 at the restores (5 escapes), msr label x latch (2), the cached ic-&gt;arg[] (M_msr_argmask), grid cov asserting G1 only -- with measured closures for the five restore-flag escapes (a session reorder) and the cached-translation mutants (a 48th loop row) — note: filed 2026-10-09 by owner ruling (&#x27;commit, file the rest&#x27;) from #562&#x27;s final pass: the Opus 5.5 seat MEASURED the escapes (regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/opus_pass2r5_20261009/KTR5_LANE1..5.out) and both closures -- the zero-observation reorder of the DPI/pop grid sessions (all five latch-clear escapes 46/47, fix 47/47; KTR5W2_*.out, probe47r.py) and the loop row (fix 48/48, M_msr_argmask 47/48, HEAD 18/48; probe48.py).  Owed together: one repair, a FULL re-table on the 48-row probe, and its own pass.  Dissent carried: deepseek, glm and kimi-k3 graded M_msr_argmask OWED; grok, codex, minimax, agy and the Opus seat graded it disclosure.  OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md carries the full entry.  Also the gate 14 parser: a dead vehicle (CONTROL=DEAD, no REDS line) is reported as malformed, and a log with one row replaced by a duplicate of another passes -- no check establishes row IDENTITY or uniqueness (the Opus seat; GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s confirmation).  ||  [2026-10-09, Fable 5.1&#x27;s #562 adjudication] ITEM: gate_arm.sh&#x27;s `arm_msrmode rows failed` check (grep -E &#x27; want=&#x27; | grep -cE &#x27; FAIL &#x27;) is green only because the probe truncates notes to 64 characters, which cuts the `kill 14` note before its &#x27; FAIL &#x27; text; a future note edit can turn the gate RED falsely -- loud, the safe direction.  Key the check on the row&#x27;s verdict column, not on free text.  ||  [2026-10-09, Fable 5.1&#x27;s regress review of #562 (regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/regress_20261009/fable5_regress562.md), notes]: `tbit` and `encl2` have no diag line -- a diag_unimpl call on each is a cheap addition for THIS repair (an AST change, so not #562&#x27;s); and `rows failed` is green only because note[:64] cuts kill 14&#x27;s note before its &#x27; FAIL &#x27; text, already filed here as the gate-parser bullet.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">headerstaleobj</span><span class="ttl">build trees: a HEADER change leaves stale objects -- the build tracks no header dependencies, propagate_all_trees.sh removes only ${F%.c}.o, and the two-part clearance ([ binary -nt source ]) cannot see an object compiled against the old header</span><span class="tip">build trees: a HEADER change leaves stale objects -- the build tracks no header dependencies, propagate_all_trees.sh removes only ${F%.c}.o, and the two-part clearance ([ binary -nt source ]) cannot see an object compiled against the old header — witness: harness:#562&#x27;s gate 14 run -- regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/gate14_20261009/gate14_run1.out (xscale ANCHOR_ISRC/ANCHOR_EXC red, 28/30) and gate14_20261009/xscale_ab.out: a HEAD build 30/30 twice, both incrementally rebuilt #562 builds 28/30 twice — note: FOUND 2026-10-09 by #562&#x27;s gate 14.  #562 inserted `uint32_t mode_warned` into struct arm_cpu (src/include/cpu_arm.h) BEFORE i80321_inten/isrc, tmr0, tmr0_irq/tmr1_irq and tisr; dev_i80321.c is the only object outside src/cpus that touches them.  Every build that rebuilt only src/cpus/*.o (the carrier&#x27;s recipe, my propagate562.sh and every kill-table clone) linked a dev_i80321.o compiled against the OLD layout, so the device set isrc at the old offset and the guest read 0 -- gate 14&#x27;s xscale anchor red on the fix and green on HEAD, deterministically.  The two-part clearance PASSED on all three trees: the binary was newer than every source.  propagate_all_trees.sh can relink and report clearance success while header-dependent objects stay stale: `rm -f ${F%.c}.o` deletes nothing for a .h and the link recipe relinks unconditionally (GPT-6 Astra&#x27;s confirmation; this note first said the tool would report the header stale -- false).  SCOPE MEASURED: only dev_i80321.c reads a field after the insertion point; cd is the last member of struct cpu, so no subsequent struct cpu member shifted, and every other non-CPU ARM access precedes the insertion; the msrmode probe drives -E testarm, which attaches no i80321, so #562&#x27;s kill-table results are unaffected.  OWED: when a propagated path is a header, delete every object (or every object that includes it) and rebuild; and a third clearance part -- no object older than any edited header -- in the tool and the checkpoint step.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-in work"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">wdc473floor</span><span class="ttl">regress/diff_wdc_identify.c: #473&#x27;s re-arm/arm clamp detector passes all 128 rows under EIGHT one-token variants (bound moves at both clamps; first-byte-only content checks), and #495&#x27;s write guard is ungated</span><span class="tip">regress/diff_wdc_identify.c: #473&#x27;s re-arm/arm clamp detector passes all 128 rows under EIGHT one-token variants (bound moves at both clamps; first-byte-only content checks), and #495&#x27;s write guard is ungated — note: filed 2026-10-09 from the late REVIEW seats on wdcrearmzero (Fable 5.1 and Opus 5.5, both MEASURED in scratch clones; regress/artifacts/wdcrearmzero/review_20261009/).  Fable: the re-arm bound relaxed to 65536 or lowered to 16384, the arm bound relaxed to 65536, the re-arm operand swapped to atapi_received -- 0 of 128 red each; rows at 32767 and 32769 on each clamp kill all four (a just-PAST row alone cannot see a LOWERED bound).  Opus: Md_frozenj (codex&#x27;s, named on #473&#x27;s pass 2, never built), Md_revwalk (glm&#x27;s), Md_halfj, Md_armfrozen -- every content check reads only the chunk&#x27;s first byte; three rows kill all four and also HEAD with #495&#x27;s write guard removed.  Clause-(d) floor breach of shipped material: L2, a FOLLOW-UP round under the late-dissent rule (disposition 2), never under #473&#x27;s number.  OWNER 2026-10-09: this round FIRST, then the asiceventaddr closure, then armmmuvehicle.</span></span><span class="state st-in work">in work</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-in work"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g