an abort taken while the active page table does not map the vector page recurses through nested prefetch aborts until the HOST process dies (SIGSEGV after ~47,591 nested faults in 10.6 s)</span><span class="tip">ARM MMU: an abort taken while the active page table does not map the vector page recurses through nested prefetch aborts until the HOST process dies (SIGSEGV after ~47,591 nested faults in 10.6 s) — note: filed 2026-10-09 from the Opus 5.5 seat&#x27;s armmmuvehicle pass-1 answer (MEASURED, regress/artifacts/armmmuvehicle/pass1_20261009/opus5/opus5_meas/meas3_base.out -- the run log, its status from waitpid -- and T3_vec_unmapped.txt, meas3.py&#x27;s head-and-tail excerpt of that transcript): unmodified -E testarm, the MMU on, section 0 through a coarse table whose page 0 is unmapped, one data abort -&gt; 47,591 nested &#x27;{ arm memory fault ...}&#x27; lines and &#x27;Exception caused no mode change?&#x27; warnings in 10.6 s (10,473,809 bytes), the process ended by signal 11; the &#x27;could not find physical address of the exception handler&#x27; exit in cpu_dyntrans.c appears ZERO times.  READ mechanism (Opus): arm_exception -&gt; quick_pc_to_pointers -&gt; the generic lookup -&gt; translate_v2p fails -&gt; arm_exception(PREF_ABT) -&gt; quick_pc_to_pointers -&gt; ... before control returns to the generic function&#x27;s second lookup.  A guest that unmaps its own vectors and takes any abort ends the host process: guest-drivable process death. The unlatched fault/warning diagnostics are also a flood (floodclass).  Vehicle: armmmuvehicle.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span clas