: X_is_held_exact 32/49, X_never_discharge 43/49 (it reds t_discharged, one of the four rows heldmasked&#x27;s closure names), X_notseat_is_answer 45/49, X_annotation_is_answer 45/49, X_nopanel_not_exempt 41/49, X_dash_tok_blank 44/49.  The thirteenth is MISLABELLED: its regex anchors on leading whitespace before t_reread, which every listing line except a VIOLATION replaces with ok/--/.., so it can only assert &#x27;t_reread is not a violation&#x27;; X_filing_is_zero (`if len(got) == 1:` -&gt; `== 0`) passes 49/49.  Shape to adopt, one commit: the seven variants, and re-pin t_reread on its `..    t_reread  review  1/9  filed` line (or rename it).</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-open"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">ofemulnodata</span><span class="ttl">src/promemul/of.c of_emul(): the OpenFirmware emulation entry calls fatal() + exit(1) when machine-&gt;md.of_data is NULL, which is true on every machine except macppc -- and the ARM and PowerPC decoders route their OpenFirmware magic instruction to it with no machine or privilege check</span><span class="tip">src/promemul/of.c of_emul(): the OpenFirmware emulation entry calls fatal() + exit(1) when machine-&gt;md.of_data is NULL, which is true on every machine except macppc -- and the ARM and PowerPC decoders route their OpenFirmware magic instruction to it with no machine or privilege check — note: filed 2026-10-16 from the adjudication of the agy pack&#x27;s second readings (packet D, H1): all three seats FILE, HIGH, own row (regress/artifacts/adj_20261016/astra/D_secondreadings/codex_adjD.txt, grok/D_secondreadings/grok_adjD.txt, fable5/fable5_adj_D_secondreadings_v2_FABLE.md).  Source: prescreen_audits5.md of_two/F9.  READ at HEAD by all three: of.c:1096-1101 (the NULL check and the exit), :1078 (the only writer, of_emul_init, called only from machine_macppc.c:99); ARM decode cpu_arm_instr.c:5034-5036 -&gt; X(openfirmware) :988-991; PowerPC decode cpu_ppc_instr.c:4400-4402 -&gt; X(openfirmware) :3956-3958.  A guest instruction therefore ends the emulator process on machines that never set up OpenFirmware.  Not covered by ofopenexit or ofpeerexit (other sites in the same file); Fable 5.1: may share one round with them.  A rung-3 ATTEMPT exists, made by claude-opus-4-8 in the Fable seat&#x27;s fallback run (so it is not a Fable ruling and owes review before it counts as the witness): regress/artifacts/adj_20261016/fable5/meas_D/witness_hostexit.py and .out, at HEAD e483d931 on the unmodified ARM test machine (the emulator prints `of_emul(): no of_data struct?&#x27; and the process exits 1), each with a benign-instruction liveness control that stays alive.</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open">