line"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">dashmissingd</span><span class="ttl">tools/pipeline/gen_dashboard.py renders an ANSWER with no `d` as the seat-failure glyph and precommit Q2 lets new ones in: 814 of 2,953 displayed answer cells at HEAD 8bf8b5a1 (682 of them, by a keyword screen, real answers)</span><span class="tip">tools/pipeline/gen_dashboard.py renders an ANSWER with no `d` as the seat-failure glyph and precommit Q2 lets new ones in: 814 of 2,953 displayed answer cells at HEAD 8bf8b5a1 (682 of them, by a keyword screen, real answers) — commits: dd2d4e01 — note: filed 2026-10-17 at the dashokclass landing, by the main loop: regress/artifacts/dashokclass_20261016/DASHMISSINGD_CENSUS_HEAD_8bf8b5a1.txt (its deriver dashmissingd_census.py beside it) counts 1,561 of 5,177 entries as answers with no d -- 2026-08 174, 2026-09 1,244, 2026-10 143, the latest dated 2026-10-16 -- and 814 displayed cells whose latest answer has none.  gen_dashboard.py&#x27;s `d = ent.get(&quot;d&quot;, &quot;…&quot;)` shows each as no answer / seat failure.  A rule question for the adjudicators, not a sweep: either Q2 refuses a NEW answer without d (reversing Astra&#x27;s condition 1 forward of a cutoff) or the renderer gives a d-less answer its own class; RULINGS_C F2 keeps the old entries as they are either way.  ENTANGLED WITH SECTION H (the same census&#x27;s NOT-FIRED screen, /not[ -]fired|roster/i, at HEAD): 222 entries record a seat not fired or name the roster, 200 untokened (answers by is_answer), 87 of them with no d, and check_stage_panels.py counts an untokened entry as a recorded seat while skipping a NOTSEAT one -- so refusing a new d-less answer would refuse the next landing&#x27;s not-fired entries, and tokening them NOTSEAT turns H red (9/9 untokened, 4/9 tokened -- GPT-6 Astra, v4 pass); the ruling must take both.  A mechanism for the owner to weigh (Fable 5.1, v4 pass): an entry-scoped &#x27;not fired by owner roster&#x27; token that is_answer treats as a non-answer, the renderer as a record and section H as roster-excused.  (The v3 pass&#x27;s &#x27;158 / 127 / 71&#x27; came from an unrecorded screen and could not be reproduced.)</span></span><span class="state st-open">open</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Research (fix proposals)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Final review (flagship adjudication)</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-open"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</spa